# tests/githist, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A CLIENT TEST — it drives `caos-cli`, so its base is `DEEP-DEPS/cli-test`
# (dev/cli-test), the image that stages a git worktree and then runs `worker1`.
#
# A CLIENT, not a worker, and that is forced rather than chosen. The subjects
# walk history by hash, so every commit they touch has to be ON THE SERVER --
# and only a client puts it there. `caos put-commit` records a commit in the
# minting worker's CAS; binding it as `--x:@=` makes a gitlink, and git
# reachability does not traverse gitlinks, so a worker-minted ancestor is
# unreachable from the tool's container. `--wc:commit=` from a client resolves
# through `ensure_pushed`, which ships the closure.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/cli-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --test:@=.
